*Unitary Matrices:* A matrix $U$ is unitary if its conjugate transpose (adjoint) is its inverse, i.e., $U^dagger U = U U^dagger = I$. This condition implies that the columns (and rows) of a unitary matrix form an orthonormal basis, meaning their inner product must satisfy $chevron.l U_i | U_j chevron.r = delta_(i j)$.
